---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CallSheet from '../components/CallSheet.astro';
import { analytics, luma, site } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this website collects about you: nothing. What Luma collects when you register, what happens to photographs taken at events, and how to ask us to remove one."
>
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="shell">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-block-start: var(--space-m)">
        Short version: this website does not collect anything about you at all. There is no
        cookie banner because there are no cookies to warn you about.
      </p>
      <div style="margin-block-start: var(--space-l)">
        <CallSheet
          label="Summary"
          rows={[
            { key: 'Cookies', val: 'None' },
            { key: 'Analytics', val: analytics.enabled ? `Yes — ${analytics.provider}, no cookies, no personal data` : 'None' },
            { key: 'Tracking', val: 'None' },
            { key: 'Your data', val: 'We hold none of it from this site' },
            { key: 'Contact', val: site.email },
          ]}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="detail">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2 id="detail">The longer version</h2>

      <h3>This website</h3>
      <p>
        Every page here is a plain file served to your browser. There are no cookies, no
        analytics scripts, no tracking pixels, no embedded fonts loaded from somebody
        else's server, no social media widgets and no advertising. Nothing you do on this
        site is recorded by us or shared with anybody.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whoever hosts the site keeps standard server logs for a short period — the sort of
        thing every web server writes down — and we do not read them or connect them to
        anybody.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is one exception, and it is the events page: the calendar is shown inside a
        frame that comes from Luma, and the "save me a spot" button loads a small piece of
        code from Luma. If you use either of those, Luma will know about it in the way any
        website you visit knows about it. Everything on this site works without them —
        there is always a plain link next to the embed.
      </p>

      <h3>Registering for an event</h3>
      <p>
        Booking is handled entirely by <a href={luma.calendarUrl} rel="noopener">Luma</a>.
        When you register, your name and email address are held by Luma, not by us. We can
        see the guest list for our own events, and we use it for exactly two things:
        knowing how many chairs to put out, and sending the occasional message about the
        event you signed up for.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell it, share it, or add you to anything else. If you want off the list,
        you can leave the calendar on Luma at any time, or{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>email us</a> and we will remove you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Luma's own privacy policy covers what they do with it:{' '}
        <a href="https://luma.com/privacy" rel="noopener">luma.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>Photographs</h3>
      <p>
        We take photographs at events and put some of them on{' '}
        <a href="/past">the archive page</a>. It is the honest record of what these
        evenings are, and it is the main reason people who have never been decide to come.
        There are none up yet, because there has not been an event yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can opt out at the door and nobody will photograph you. If a photograph of you
        is already up and you would rather it was not, email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with a rough description of which
        one — you do not have to explain why, and we will take it down, usually the same
        day and always within a week.
      </p>

      <h3>Email</h3>
      <p>
        If you email us, we keep the email so we can reply and so we remember the
        conversation. Ask us to delete it and we will.
      </p>

      <h3>Your rights</h3>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law you can ask what we hold about you, ask for it to be
        corrected, or ask for it to be deleted. Write to{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will sort it out — there is
        no form and no process. If you are not happy with how we handle it, you can
        complain to the{' '}
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">Information
        Commissioner's Office</a>.
      </p>

      <h3>If this changes</h3>
      <p>
        If we ever turn on privacy-respecting, cookie-free visitor counting, this page gets
        updated before it goes live rather than after. It is currently{' '}
        <strong>{analytics.enabled ? 'on' : 'off'}</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
